% Obligation: 0 - x == ~x + 1, for every 64-bit word x.
% This is the identity the code generator RELIES ON for unary minus, and the one
% money.bp's negation path assumes when it builds a refund that must net to
% exactly zero. It is stated over `sub`, which no committed obligation used
% before: bb_sub64 is a + ~b + 1 as TWO adds, so a certificate for this is also
% the first evidence that the subtractor's own decomposition is the one the
% checker blasts.
obligation neg_is_not_plus_one
1 var x
2 const 0
3 sub 2 1
4 not 1
5 const 1
6 add 4 5
7 eq 3 6
prove 7
